# Android app configuration template (Secrets Gradle Plugin).
#
# The Secrets plugin is configured to read this file; on this branch it
# supplies NO BuildConfig fields (no provider secret of any kind).
#
# SECURITY NOTE (Phase 8.7-C / 8.7-C.1 / 8.7-C.3):
# Values compiled into the APK are recoverable from the distributed
# artifact and MUST NOT include reusable provider secrets.
# GEMINI_API_KEY has been REMOVED from the app:
#
#   * Android-distributed applications cannot keep a reusable provider
#     secret confidential.
#   * On this branch Android repository analysis is OFFLINE-ONLY: the app
#     always runs its deterministic, non-secret on-device template engine.
#     No remote analysis path exists.
#   * A future server-side Gemini integration is NOT implemented on this
#     branch; it may only be described as current behavior once a real,
#     authenticated backend contract is implemented and verified here.
#   * The gateway URL in Android settings is a reachability diagnostic
#     only — it does not route analysis, Gemini requests, deployments, or
#     execution.
#   * The Gemini key belongs in the SERVER-SIDE environment of the
#     platform (devops-ai-platform / backend services), never in this file.
#
# No key means the app truthfully runs its offline template engine (no
# live AI) instead of falling back to a bundled credential.
